From: Asius <contact@asius.ai>
Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom: tzmem: share Dragon EL2 buffers with their caller

Dragon U-Boot uses Secure Launch to enter EL2. A bridge granting only HLOS
access is accepted, but storage SMC calls return SMC_ERR_BUF_PTR_NOT_NS.
A self-owner-only bridge allows INIT but GET_INFO still fails. Granting
both HLOS and the current caller access makes GET_INFO work.

Limit this firmware quirk to Dragon boots with EL2 available. Keep the
existing HLOS mapping and grant read/write, without execute permission.
The default behavior remains unchanged for stock EL1 boots and other
boards. The storage interface and its transfer limit remain separate
upstream-derived patches.

--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_tzmem.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_tzmem.c
@@ -72,7 +72,13 @@
 #include <linux/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.h>
 #include <linux/of.h>
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_ARM64
+#include <asm/virt.h>
+#endif
+
 #define QCOM_SHM_BRIDGE_NUM_VM_SHIFT 9
+#define QCOM_SHM_BRIDGE_SELF_OWNER BIT(1)
+#define QCOM_SHM_BRIDGE_SELF_OWNER_PERM_SHIFT 2
 
 static bool qcom_tzmem_using_shm_bridge;
 
@@ -134,6 +140,17 @@
 	pfn_and_ns_perm = paddr | QCOM_SCM_PERM_RW;
 	ipfn_and_s_perm = paddr | QCOM_SCM_PERM_RW;
 	size_and_flags = size | (1 << QCOM_SHM_BRIDGE_NUM_VM_SHIFT);
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_ARM64
+	/*
+	 * Dragon Secure Launch replaces Gunyah with our EL2 boot context.
+	 * TrustZone then checks caller access as well as HLOS access for
+	 * nested storage buffers. Keep HLOS and add the current owner.
+	 */
+	if (of_machine_is_compatible("radxa,dragon-q6a") && is_hyp_mode_available())
+		size_and_flags |= QCOM_SHM_BRIDGE_SELF_OWNER |
+			((u64)QCOM_SCM_PERM_RW << QCOM_SHM_BRIDGE_SELF_OWNER_PERM_SHIFT);
+#endif
 
 	ret = qcom_scm_shm_bridge_create(pfn_and_ns_perm, ipfn_and_s_perm,
 					 size_and_flags, QCOM_SCM_VMID_HLOS,
